I'm Christy Turlington burns and I'm the  founder of every mother counts women die  from pregnancy and childbirth  complications around the world everyday  800 women per day so this organization  was founded as a way to educate people  about the challenges and the solutions  and to engage those people to  participate in becoming part of a  solution  90% of those deaths are preventable and  that's the part that I think when I  learned that made me see that this is  one of those things that we can do a  better job we're not looking for a cure  giving birth is the most natural thing  in the world  however 15 percent of all pregnancies  will result in a complication and so  access to people and services is  critical for every woman going through  this experience in the event that she  should have a complication to prevent  these unnecessary deaths is possible so  by educating mid-level providers  midwives nurses health workers community  health workers by making sure that women  are linked to a health care system in  that through these health workers that  should they see signs of complications  that they have access transportation  access to other services that might  require more medical interventions and  and information education and  information about one's body and sexual  reproductive health is critical to so  many women are vulnerable because they  don't know anything about how their  bodies work they're not told what signs  to look for they don't understand that  they can't do this on their own and so  information and education from both the  public as well as the individual sort of  you know woman going through the  experience and making that connection so  that women feel supported in that time  is really our goal  I was an entrepreneur in the business  space before I was an entrepreneur in  the nonprofit space and so I would say  it's a very similar experience the  difference is that in the end I'm not  selling a product per se it's a it's  it's sharing a tragedy that people can  connect with and trying to invite them  in to be a part of a solution and so for  me as an entrepreneur in this area it's  just very different in the sense that  there's number that there's there's  never that sort of you know this will do  this it's very clear that the things  that we're sort of inviting people to  share are things that make sense they're  things that anyone would wish to have  and want to have going through  childbirth and so it's more about  educating the public and then inviting  them in to participate in something  together
 

